==Icelandic==

===Etymology 1===
From Old Norse {{term|ríða||to ride|lang=non}} from {{Ger.|ang}} ''*ridanan'', from {{IE.|ang}} ''*reidh-''. Cognate Old English {{term|rida||to ride|lang=ang}}, English {{term|ride|lang=en}} and German {{term|reiten|lang=de}}.

====Verb====
'''ríða''' (+ {{accusative}}/{{dat}})

# to [[ride]] (esp. on [[horseback]])
#: ''[[ekki#Icelandic|Ekki]] '''ríða''' [[hestur#Icelandic|hestinum]] [[minn#Icelandic|mínum]].''
#:: Don't '''ride''' my [[horse]].
#: ''Að fara '''ríðandi'''.''
#:: To '''go on''' horseback.
# {{vulgar|lang=is}} to [[fuck]], to [[have sex]] with
#: ''[[langa#Icelandic|Langar]] [[þú#Icelandic|þig]] að '''ríða'''?''
#:: Do you [[want]] to '''fuck'''?
#: [[w:is:Ríddu mér|'''''Ríddu''' mér]].''
#:: [[w:en:Baise-moi|'''Fuck''' me]].

=====Derived terms=====
* [[ríða á miklu]] (to be very important)
* [[ríða á vaðið]] (to [[take the first step]])
* [[ríða af]] (especially of shots and bullets; to be [[fired]])
*: ''Skotið '''reið af'''.''
*:: The shot was '''fired'''.
* [[aldan reið yfir]] (the [[wave]] broke)
* [[ríða af sér]] (+{{accusative}}, to ride away from sby, to ride faster than another)
* [[ríða að fullu]] (to [[exhaust]], to finish somebody off)
* [[ríða burtreið]] ("[[tilt]]", "[[joust]]")
* [[reið]]

=====Usage notes=====
* Because the word denotes both the meaning of ''riding an animal'' and ''fucking'', it is often a the subject of [[double entendre]] [[bestiality]] jokes.

===Etymology 2===

====Verb====
'''ríða''' (+ {{accusative}}) ([[reið]], [[riðu]], [[riðið]])

# to [[knot]]
#: ''Að '''ríða''' hnút.''
#:: To '''tie''' a knot.
# to [[braid]] og [[weave]]
#: ''Að '''ríða''' körfu.''
#:: To '''weave''' a basket.
#: ''Að '''ríða''' net.''
#:: To '''weave''' a net.

